coder › Implemented `wrap(text, width)` in `src/wrap.ts` and added tests in `src/wrap.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `src/wrap.ts`: replaced the not-implemented stub with a greedy word-wrap implementation:
  - Normalizes CRLF/CR to LF, splits input on blank lines (`/\n\s*\n/`) into paragraphs.
  - Splits each paragraph on `/\s+/` (so runs of spaces/tabs/newlines within a paragraph count as one) and packs words greedily with single spaces.
  - Words longer than `width` are split across lines (including filling the remainder of a partially-filled line).
  - Non-empty paragraphs are joined back with exactly one blank line; leading/trailing/extra blank lines produce no extra output.
  - Lines are built without trailing spaces; output is `lines.join("\n")`.
  - `width < 1` (including 0, negatives, NaN) throws `RangeError` via `if (!(width >= 1))`.
- `src/wrap.test.ts`: 11 tests covering fit-on-one-line, breaking at spaces with no line over width, greedy packing, space-run collapsing, single-newline-as-space, long-word splitting, one-blank-line paragraph separation, per-paragraph wrapping, empty/blank input → `""`, no-trailing-space + width invariant, and `RangeError` on width < 1.

Decisions not in the plan: CRLF/CR normalized to LF; a line containing only whitespace counts as a blank-line separator; tabs and single newlines inside a paragraph treated as word breaks; empty/whitespace-only input returns `""` rather than blank lines.

Checks:
- `bun test`: `11 pass, 0 fail, 39 expect() calls, Ran 11 tests across 1 file.`
- `tsc --noEmit --strict` on `src/wrap.ts`: exit 0, no errors. (`src/wrap.test.ts` alone reports `TS2307: Cannot find module 'bun:test'` under plain tsc without bun types, which is expected; no tsconfig in repo.)
- No lint configured (`package.json` only has `test: bun test`).

